##CauseOfFailure=VCFv4.3.tex line 121: "All structured lines require an ID which must be unique within their type, i.e., within all the meta-information lines with the same `##key=` prefix." -- this ##FILTER declaration's ID= attribute is present but empty, which VCFv4.3+'s ID requirement is not satisfied by either. See DUPLICATE_METADATA_ID_HANDLING.md's "Empty/whitespace ID is a deliberate stricter-than-bcftools choice" section: vcf-parser treats an empty ID= the same as a missing one, a deliberate editorial decision no spec version addresses.
##ExpectParser=warn
##Authority=VCFv4.3.tex line 121 (quoted above), plus DUPLICATE_METADATA_ID_HANDLING.md's "Empty/whitespace ID is a deliberate stricter-than-bcftools choice" section for why an empty ID is treated identically to a missing one even though bcftools itself does not (see below).
##Authority=bcftools 1.23.1 (htslib 1.23.1) keeps the declaration verbatim with NO warning at all, exit 0 -- BcftoolsDependencyTest#testFilterEmptyIdBcftoolsKeepsVerbatim pins this live measurement; re-confirmed directly via bcftools view -h on 2026-08-16. This is inconsistent within bcftools itself -- ##FILTER's own missing-ID case (see the sibling filter-missing-id.vcf fixture) is silently dropped, but an empty ID= is tolerated -- vcf-parser instead drops the declaration entirely for both cases, a deliberate stricter-than-bcftools choice.
